==French==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|fr}} {{m|la|sortīrī}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|sortior}}, possibly influenced by a derivative of ''[[surgō]]''. Compare Italian ''[[sortire]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-sortie.ogg|audio|lang=fr}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|f}}

# An [[exit]] or [[way out]].
# The action of exiting or going out of a place.
# The [[end]]; final part of.
# The [[release]] of a film, book, album etc.
# A school [[outing]] or [[trip]] lasting no longer than a day.
# {{context|military|lang=fr}} [[leave|Leave]], [[sally]], [[#English|sortie]]

====Usage notes====
* The meaning "end, release" is used of things such as school, theater etc. where a literal "exit" also occurs.

